<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The launcher icon's foreground layer: the Flow A.

  ## Generated from the canonical mark, not redrawn

  `pathData` and `strokeWidth` below are byte-for-byte the `d` and
  `stroke-width` of `docs/design/assets/logo-flow-a.svg`, which is the same
  geometry `docs/design/assets/app-icon.svg` carries and the same one
  `desktop/gui/tests/brand_assets.rs` pins for the desktop. One mark, one path,
  three platforms. `BrandingResourcesTest` asserts the equality, so the two
  cannot drift a curve at a time.

  ## Why the group only moves it

  An adaptive icon is drawn on a 108x108 canvas of which a launcher may show
  as little as the inner 72x72 square — or, for a round mask, only a 66-unit
  circle about the centre. The mark is 55.78 x 56.00 units wide once its
  8-unit round-capped stroke is counted, which fits inside *both* of those at
  its native size, so this group scales by exactly 1 and does nothing but
  translate.

  That is worth more than it looks. At scale 1 the numbers in this file are
  the numbers in the SVG: the stroke is 8 units here and 8 units there, so
  "the stroke weight is the family" (BRAND.md) is preserved by arithmetic
  rather than by someone remembering to rescale it.

  ## The placement, and how it was chosen

  The ink's minimum enclosing circle has its centre at (32.81, 36.24) on the
  64-unit grid and a radius of 32.25 — *not* the centre of the bounding box,
  because the A's apex and its out-flung crossbar terminal are not
  symmetrical. Translating by (21.2, 17.8) lands that circle's centre on the
  canvas centre (54, 54), which is the placement that buys the most clearance
  from a round mask:

      66-unit round safe zone   r_max 32.29 of 33      0.71 to spare
      72x72 square safe zone    ink [21.80, 82.20]     3.80 to spare

  Both are asserted by `BrandingResourcesTest`, recomputed from this file's
  own path and group rather than trusted from this comment.

  The Android 12+ splash screen inherits the same margin for free: it shows
  the inner two thirds of this foreground, which is the same 72-of-108 the
  square safe zone already answers for.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:aapt="http://schemas.android.com/aapt"
    android:width="108dp" android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108" android:viewportHeight="108">
    <group android:translateX="21.2" android:translateY="17.8">
        <path
            android:pathData="M 53 56 C 50 41 43 22 32 8 C 22 21 15 36 10 47 C 7.5 52.5 11.5 56.5 15.5 52 C 22 43.5 33 38 45 37.5 C 50 37.3 54 38 57 39"
            android:strokeWidth="8"
            android:strokeLineCap="round"
            android:strokeLineJoin="round">
            <aapt:attr name="android:strokeColor">
                <gradient android:type="linear"
                    android:startX="10" android:startY="56"
                    android:endX="54" android:endY="8">
                    <item android:offset="0" android:color="#FF16B8A6" />
                    <item android:offset="0.5" android:color="#FF4F7CFF" />
                    <item android:offset="1" android:color="#FF8B5CF6" />
                </gradient>
            </aapt:attr>
        </path>
    </group>
</vector>
